nodecode-wolfmarkdown is a rewrite of WolfMarkTools's WolfMarkTools/WolfMarkDown:

  https://github.com/WolfMarkTools/WolfMarkDown
  commit d9c1b4a7e31df41ed1e555f5d7c0a8f27e16c5ad
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 WolfMark Tools (LICENSE)

The original is a skill plus a Node toolchain: a SKILL.md that tells an agent when to compose, clean and verify a Markdown file, five scripts over markdownlint, Prettier and a GFM parser, and reference guides for composing, preservation and semantic repair. This rewrite keeps the part a user can check for themselves and puts it in the image: the structure checks (fences, heading depth, table shape, frontmatter, whitespace, list markers, adjacent citations), the protected-token integrity comparison against an untouched snapshot, the ordered-sequence and ledger-record preservation checks, and the canonical-format rewrite with the citation repair as its one safe fix. All of it is Common Lisp over the text, offered as three tools and a /markdown command.

Left out: the Node runtime and its dependencies (markdownlint 0.41.1, Prettier 3.9.9, remark 15, yaml 2.9.1) and with them Prettier's exact byte-level formatting, markdownlint's full rule set and a real GFM parse; the doctor, install and scaffold scripts, since there is nothing to install and the source map is a tool here; the discovery symlinks under ~/.agents/skills and ~/.claude/skills, which belong to a harness that loads skills from folders; and the reference guides, whose workflow is carried in the tools' own descriptions.
